    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nOccupying a highly sought-after position on Church Hill in the heart of Wicklow Town, this impressive late Victorian residence presents a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial period home brimming with character, charm and untapped potential. Enjoying views towards the historic church and set amidst mature gardens, the property combines an enviable location with generous accommodation and elegant architectural features.\n\nThe attractive façade immediately reflects the home's Victorian heritage, while a sweeping driveway provides ample off-street parking and a welcoming approach. The surrounding gardens are mature and well-established, offering privacy, colour and scope for further enhancement.\n\nExtending to spacious and versatile accommodation, the property comprises four well-proportioned bedrooms and four elegant reception rooms, providing exceptional living and entertaining space. The kitchen is complemented by a practical utility room, while a ground-floor shower room and a main family bathroom serve the household's needs.\n\nThroughout the property, many original period features remain, offering a wonderful opportunity for a discerning purchaser to restore and enhance this fine home while preserving its historic character. The generous room proportions, high ceilings and abundance of natural light are characteristic of the Victorian era and create a sense of grandeur rarely found in modern homes.\n\nThe property has been vacant for approximately two years and may qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, subject to the relevant terms, conditions and approvals. While the residence would benefit from modernisation and refurbishment, it offers tremendous potential to create a magnificent family home in one of Wicklow Town's most desirable residential settings.\n\nIdeally located within walking distance of the town centre, harbour, schools, shops, cafés and transport links, this distinctive period property offers a unique combination of heritage, space, convenience and future potential."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Porch - 2.50m x 1.88m\nFeaturing tiled flooring and a wood panelled ceiling.\n\nEntrance Hall - 6.82m x 1.74m\nInviting entrance hallway with carpet flooring underfoot and a coved ceiling with ornate cornice.\n\nDrawing Room - 5.01m x 4.14m\nThe elegant drawing room is a wonderfully proportioned reception space, rich in period character and charm. A striking ornate ceiling with intricate decorative detailing provides an impressive focal point, and an attractive open fireplace creates a warm and inviting atmosphere. Double doors lead seamlessly through to the adjoining dining room, creating an ideal flow for both everyday family living and formal entertaining.\n\nDining Room - 4.30m x 4.17m\nLocated off the drawing room.\n\nStudy - 3.04m x 2.57m\nStudy nook postioned at the end of the entrance hall ideal for use as a home office.\n\nGuest Cloakroom - \nLocated off the hall with wc and whb.\n\nShower Room - 1.74m x 1.70m\nLocated off the utilty room with shower, wc and whb.\n\nKitchen/Breakfast Room - 6.25m x 4.80m\nSpacious kitchen featuring a range of solid wood wall and floor units and ample countertop space for food prep. For the enthusiastic chef there is an impressive Aga and there is plumbing in place for a dishwasher. The utility area is easily accessed from here and there is also access to the additional reception areas to the right wing of the house.\n\nUtilty Room - 2.63m x 2.50m\nSpacious utility area featuring a range of cupboards for storage and plumbing in place for a washer/dryer. There is a large drying rack for clothing and there is also access from here to the gardens.\n\nFamily Room - 6.25m x 4.80m\nFeaturing wood flooring.\n\nPlay Room - 3.69m x 2.81m\nFeaturing wood flooring.\n\nLanding - 4.26m x 1.76m\n\n\nBathroom - 2.85m x 2.57m\nSpacious family bathroom featuring a standalone bath with shower attachment, wc and whb.\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.59m x 4.17m\nLocated to the rear of the house with carpet flooring.\n\nBedroom 2 - 5.01m x 4.00m\nLocated to the front of the house with an attractive bay window and carpet flooring.\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.16m x 3.75m\nFeaturing carpet flooring.\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.67m x 1.76m\nFeaturing carpet flooring.\n\n"
      },
